## 13. Implemented local qualification and production handoff

The Windows implementation uses plan version `trajectory-throw-v2-local-3` and
runtime contract `v2-data-generation-spec-3+temporal-2`. The authoritative
catalog is generated by `Scripts/v2_catalog.py`; its frozen base and sequence
fingerprints, counts, stable IDs, temporal profiles, and 128 audit slots are
covered by `Scripts/test_v2_planner.py`.

`Scripts/v2_dataset_controller.py` implements immutable qualification and
production plans, stable prefixes, exact 55/45 and 15/10/8/6/6 credited-frame
allocation, disjoint train/evaluation replay identities, bounded reserves,
assignment waves, inventory reconstruction, and source fingerprints. Production
planning refuses an unqualified duration calibration unless an explicit
diagnostic override is supplied. It also rejects X below the calibrated
complete-coverage floor. Qualification does not choose or execute production X.

Qualification supports one complete plan. The definitive local evidence split
the long random cells from the mission/sequence cells so progress could be
monitored and resumed independently:

```powershell
python Scripts/dataset_worker.py Artifacts/V2MissionSequenceDefinitive/plan `
  --executable Saved/PackagedV2Local/Windows/he_grenade_game.exe `
  --worker-id 0 --executor-id local-windows-mission-sequence-definitive
python Scripts/dataset_worker.py Artifacts/V2RandomDefinitive/plan `
  --executable Saved/PackagedV2Local/Windows/he_grenade_game.exe `
  --worker-id 0 --executor-id local-windows-random-definitive
python Scripts/v2_calibration.py `
  Artifacts/V2DefinitiveCalibration/calibration.json `
  Artifacts/V2MissionSequenceDefinitive/plan `
  Artifacts/V2RandomDefinitive/plan
```

The worker command is repeated for the plan's bounded assignment waves. Every
assignment is finalized to lossless WebP and typed Parquet, revalidated, and
published through an immutable result before it can contribute qualification
evidence. The first worker freezes an `execution-build.json` hash over the
bootstrap executable and all runtime EXE/DLL/config/package files; later
attempts reject a different package. `Scripts/v2_calibration.py` qualifies the checked-in conservative
duration minima only when all 1,184 base IDs and all 21 sequence IDs have
semantically accepted evidence.

The definitive local 64x64 qualification completed on 2026-08-09. Mission and
sequence plan `v2qualification-fdf741c861b5ef6e` validated 1,133 recipes in 95
assignments; random plan `v2qualification-67bddd117206cb1a` validated 72 recipes
in six assignments. The combined evidence has 1,205 accepted episodes, exact
1,184/1,184 base-cell coverage, exact 21/21 sequence coverage, zero semantic
failures, and zero technical failures. The merged realized report reconstructs
248,408 credited observations and zero train/evaluation replay overlap from the
validated shards.

The contract-2 `Scripts/movement_v2_duration_calibration.json` was the qualified measured
calibration `v2-local-qualified-3a4fd61cf86f9e06`, not a provisional estimate.
Its conservative family minima are random 901, solid 110, wall 108, floor 90,
ramp 105, and hoop 116 observations; sequence minima for two/three/four/five
grenades are 233/330/437/1501. The calibrated complete-coverage floor is 402,200
credited observations. Contract 3 changes random tails and adds short,
event-relative active continuation to missions, so this calibration and its 402,200
floor are historical evidence only until the complete contract-3 qualification
derives replacements.

Focused review uses a separate 384x384 `qualification-plan --audit-cells` run.
`Scripts/v2_audit.py` selects exactly the frozen 128 successful cell identities,
exports MP4s strictly from their stored observations, and writes a manifest,
coverage report, README, and family contact sheets. Each manifest row retains
the catalog cell, continuous stratum, temporal profiles, immutable plan/replay
identity, source image keys, Q edges, E request/accept edges, contact, rest, and
tail indices. Incomplete or semantically failed selections cannot be presented
as a complete audit. `Scripts/v2_report.py` reconstructs the broader realized
distribution report and can optionally decode observations for exact and
perceptual duplicate counts.

The contract-2 focused plan structurally validated all 128/128 audit slots with the frozen
18/24/16/32/24/14 random/solid/wall/floor/ramp/hoop selection. Nine additional
representative sequences (SQ03, SQ04, SQ05, SQ06, SQ07, SQ11, SQ13, SQ15, SQ20)
also validated at 384x384. The exported audit is
`Artifacts/V2VisualAudit128Definitive`; sequence MP4s are in
`Artifacts/V2SequenceReviewVideosDefinitive`. Stored frames were visually
checked at preview, throw, contact, rest/tail, hoop passage, camera relocation,
and multi-grenade persistence boundaries. Corrected smoke and R08 diagnostics
are in `Artifacts/V2DiagnosticsCorrected`, both with
`accepted_for_balancing=false`. Subsequent human video review rejected the audit
because many random recipes contained a short designated event followed by
40-70 seconds of zero input, fixed camera motion, or ineffective wall contact.

Contract 3 requires Movement-V1-style semi-Markov continuation with V2 Q/camera
activity and collision escape. An ordinary mission continues for a deterministic
1.5-3 seconds after its validated grenade/rest event, a multi-throw sequence for
2-4 seconds, and event-focused random play for 2-5 seconds after its designated
event. Only dedicated free exploration remains 45-75 seconds. Escape actions never hold Q
because aim lock would suppress the required planar movement. Validation rejects
inactive zero/fixed-action runs over five seconds, continuous player contact over
one second, missing action/camera/Q diversity, absent mission continuation, and
plan/runtime contract mismatch. Focused 384x384 evidence for R02, R13, R18, and
a direct rectangle mission passes at
`Artifacts/V2RandomContinuationFix384Contract3d`; complete catalog and visual
requalification are still required. The subsequent event-relative focused run
at `Artifacts/V2EventRelativeDuration384` validates the same four cells at
4.45/11.75/19.10/8.90 seconds total and 3.50/4.95/2.40/2.70 seconds of active
continuation, eliminating the old fixed-duration padding.

The prior 1,112 ordinary mission episodes measured 6.92 seconds mean, 6.80
seconds median, and 4.45-9.00 seconds range. Contract 3 therefore appends a
short event-relative continuation rather than padding every recipe to a long
random-play duration.

After qualification, a user-provided feasible X can be planned locally with:

```powershell
